  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.15.0-preview.2: Portability + packaging fixes. The bundled nginx + module now target a glibc 2.31 floor with statically-linked libstdc++ and no OpenSSL host dependency, so they load on Debian 11/12, Ubuntu 20.04+, RHEL/Alma 8/9 and Amazon Linux 2023 (preview.1 required GLIBC_2.38 and would not load on the default .NET 8 base image). The package now auto-pulls its native engine (a single `dotnet add package` brings the nginx+module), the binaries are stripped (debug symbols archived separately), and the bundled THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES/NOTICE/LICENSE now correctly describe the 1.15 sidecar. mod_pagespeed 1.15 as an ASP.NET Core sidecar that runs a bundled, matched (nginx + ngx_pagespeed) reverse proxy in front of your Kestrel app (ADR-085). Linux-only (linux-x64, linux-arm64). Experimental preview; API may change before GA.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
  "title": "WeAmp.PageSpeed Sidecar for ASP.NET Core — mod_pagespeed 1.15 via a bundled nginx reverse proxy",
